From 5ecd1db576fa7cf2309bbd3cce7c2b099a25aea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaorenex1 <24537608z@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:37:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 0020 Let a memory plugin stop the host loading its own memory files

A memory provider's own cards and recall are injected alongside the built-in
MEMORY.md and USER.md blocks, so the same facts ride the prompt twice and the model reads two
stores that can disagree.

``memory.minir.block_builtin_memory`` now resolves through
``get_builtin_memory_store_flags``, the one function ``agent_init`` and the memory tool's
availability check both read. The plugin owns the switch: it defaults on inside
``memory.minir``, and that block is the opt-in. A host without the plugin, or one that selected
a different provider, keeps both files; ``MINIR_BLOCK_BUILTIN_MEMORY`` overrides the stored
value, matching the plugin's env-wins contract. The plugin declares the key in its
``get_config_schema``, so ``hermes memory setup`` writes it with the rest of the block.

Blocking at the flags means no ``MemoryStore`` is constructed and ``load_from_disk`` never
runs: the files are not read, not snapshotted, and not rendered, and the ``memory`` tool
leaves the surface instead of dispatching against ``store=None``.
